The unit files the packages ship, copied verbatim for tools/sandbox-check
score: the boundary drop-ins under system/etc/systemd/system are scored
offline against these with systemd-analyze security, so the test needs
neither the packages nor root. A copy lags its package on purpose; the
score is a property of "shipped unit + our drop-in" and a pinned copy
keeps it deterministic. Refresh a copy when the package's unit changes
(pacman -Qo names the package; diff against /usr/lib/systemd/system).

